s="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGUMA, MASATO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MASUDA, HARUHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO BAKELITE CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIGUMA MASATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MASUDA HARUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGUMA, MASATO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MASUDA, HARUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A pressurizing unit (17, 20) and a distal device (1) are connected via a fluid circuit so as to infuse a fluid into the distal device (1) and the fluid circuit is provided with a control device (10, 11) for controlling the movement of ligating rings (13). The control device (10, 11) detects a pressure drop within the distal device (1) occurring when one or a plurality of ligating rings (13) disengage from the distal device (1) and stops the movement of the ligating rings (13) according the pressure drop so as to allow at least two ligating rings to disengage in a desired number at a time, thereby permitting a continuous ligating treatment on a varicosity or a hemorrhoid.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Une unité (17, 20) sous pression et un dispositif distal (1) sont reliés par un circuit fluide de manière à pouvoir introduire un liquide dans le dispositif distal (1). Le circuit de liquide est muni d'un système (10, 11) de commande des déplacements des anneaux de ligature (13), détectant les baisses de pression dans le dispositif distal (1) se produisant lorsqu'un ou plusieurs des anneaux de ligature s'en détachent, et arrêtant le mouvement des anneaux de ligature (13) lors de ces baisses de pression, ce qui permet de détacher plusieurs anneaux en même temps et de ligaturer en continu les varicosités ou hémorroïdes.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>